---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const editorialSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": "Editorial Guidelines & Quality Standards — Online Linux Terminal",
  "url": "https://onlinelinuxterminal.com/editorial-guidelines/",
  "description": "Editorial standards, fact-checking methodology, code verification workflows, and correction policies of Online Linux Terminal.",
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Online Linux Terminal",
    "url": "https://onlinelinuxterminal.com",
    "logo": "https://onlinelinuxterminal.com/icon.svg"
  }
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Guidelines & Standards — Online Linux Terminal"
  description="Our editorial process, technical fact-checking methodology, and quality assurance standards for Linux command references and tutorials."
  keywords="online linux terminal editorial guidelines, linux documentation standards, technical fact checking, eeat linux standards"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(editorialSchema)} />

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 space-y-10 text-zinc-300">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="space-y-3 border-b border-zinc-800 pb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-950/80 border border-emerald-800/80 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-mono">
        <span>Editorial Integrity & Quality Assurance</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-zinc-100 font-sans">
        Editorial Guidelines & Quality Standards
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        How we research, write, verify, and maintain high-quality Linux command manuals and interactive tutorials.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Content Sections -->
    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-8">
      
      <!-- 1. Core Principles -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-zinc-100 font-sans flex items-center space-x-2">
          <span class="text-emerald-400">1.</span>
          <span>Our Core Editorial Principles</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          At <strong>Online Linux Terminal</strong>, our goal is to provide the clearest, most technically accurate, and immediately actionable command-line documentation on the web. We adhere to three core editorial principles:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 not-prose">
          <div class="p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-800 rounded-xl space-y-1.5">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-emerald-400 text-sm">1. Empirical Accuracy</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400">Every command syntax, option flag, and error explanation is cross-checked against POSIX standards and live GNU coreutils manuals.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-800 rounded-xl space-y-1.5">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-emerald-400 text-sm">2. Real-World Practicality</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400">We prioritize authentic DevOps and sysadmin workflows over theoretical jargon, providing examples you can run immediately.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-800 rounded-xl space-y-1.5">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-emerald-400 text-sm">3. Zero-Friction Interactivity</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400">Every single guide includes a 1-click "Run in Sandbox ⚡" deep link so learners can see outputs live without local setup.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Four-Step Verification Protocol -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-zinc-100 font-sans flex items-center space-x-2">
          <span class="text-emerald-400">2.</span>
          <span>Our 4-Step Technical Verification Protocol</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          Before any command manual, tutorial, or challenge scenario is published on our platform, it undergoes a strict 4-step quality assurance workflow:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="p-4 bg-zinc-900/40 border border-zinc-800 rounded-xl space-y-1">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-zinc-200">Step 1: Primary Source Research</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400">
              Authors reference official Linux man-pages (<code>man7.org</code>), GNU coreutils documentation, POSIX IEEE Std 1003.1, and kernel documentation to define exact flag behaviors.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-zinc-900/40 border border-zinc-800 rounded-xl space-y-1">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-zinc-200">Step 2: Live Shell & Sandbox Validation</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400">
              Every code snippet and command pipe is executed both in native Linux environments (Ubuntu 24.04 LTS / Debian 12) and inside our browser AST terminal to ensure behavioral parity and exact output matching.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-zinc-900/40 border border-zinc-800 rounded-xl space-y-1">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-zinc-200">Step 3: Peer Review by DevOps Practitioners</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400">
              Content is reviewed by experienced systems administrators to evaluate edge cases, permission caveats, and security implications (e.g., highlighting why <code>chmod 777</code> is a security hazard).
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-zinc-900/40 border border-zinc-800 rounded-xl space-y-1">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-zinc-200">Step 4: Continuous Audits & Feedback Integration</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400">
              We monitor user feedback, browser execution logs, and upstream GNU release notes to refresh documentation when flags or best practices evolve.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. AI & Content Integrity -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-zinc-100 font-sans flex items-center space-x-2">
          <span class="text-emerald-400">3.</span>
          <span>Content Integrity & Anti-Hallucination Policy</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          We believe technical documentation must never contain speculative or untested information. While modern tools may assist in drafting, <strong>every single command line flag, syntax block, and error explanation published on this website is manually reviewed and empirically verified by human engineers</strong>. We prohibit hallucinated command options and unverified scripts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Corrections Policy -->
      <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-zinc-800 pt-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-zinc-100 font-sans flex items-center space-x-2">
          <span class="text-emerald-400">4.</span>
          <span>Corrections & Community Reporting</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          We are committed to swift transparency. If you discover a typo, an outdated flag description, or an edge-case bug in our simulated environment, please submit a correction report:
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-800 rounded-xl space-y-2 text-xs font-mono">
          <div><strong class="text-zinc-200">Editorial Inquiries:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@onlinelinuxterminal.com" class="text-emerald-400 hover:underline">support@onlinelinuxterminal.com</a></div>
          <div><strong class="text-zinc-200">Correction Turnaround:</strong> Typically reviewed and updated within 24–48 hours.</div>
          <div><strong class="text-zinc-200">GitHub Repository:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/NomanMohammadOfficial/OnlineLinuxTerminal" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-emerald-400 hover:underline">github.com/NomanMohammadOfficial/OnlineLinuxTerminal</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
